-  code %/main

"spaced repetition: cards, decks, and the review clock"

=  recall
  '  when next (an epoch nat, supplied with the grade), gap width
  '  (days), ease (x1000)
  !  srs/due n
  !  srs/interval n
  !  srs/ease n

=  card recall
  '  a card is recall metadata plus the prompt: front/back text of
  '  its own, or about pointing at any namespace node whose content
  '  is the prompt
  !  front t | about path
  ?  back t

=  deck
  !  title t

#  finish_card
  '  mark a card with its review feedback: grade (0 again, 1 hard,
  '  2 good, 3 easy) and when (the review time, stamped by the /op
  '  route) poke together; the review behavior computes the next
  '  schedule in the same event and consumes the grade
  :  recall
  >
    :  srs/grade  n
    :  when  n
  <
    recall

:  op ./op/finish_card
:  sys/face 'h;z;%/weft/page

+  cards
  *  ts card
  +  what_is_a_shrine_name card
    "the starter card"
    :  front "What does a Shrine name identify?"
    :  back "A versioned locus of state."
    :  srs/due 0
    :  srs/interval 0
    :  srs/ease 2500
+  decks
  *  ts deck
+  next
  "the review queue: a spun view over the cards, limit at a time"
  :  weft code#next
  :  limit 10
  :  tack '?/y;%/cards
+  weft
  +  page
    "the srs face component"
    :  weft code#srs_html
    :  sys/lede "the srs interface: the due queue at the root, reveal and grade per card"
    :  demo ./cards/what_is_a_shrine_name
